","To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, follow these steps:  
1. **Convert the percentage to a fraction**:  
   0.044% = 0.044/100 = 0.0044  
2. **Interpret the (w/v) notation**:  
   (w/v) means weight of solute per volume of solution.  
   The concentration is 0.044 g of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of Phos-Flur Rinse.  
3. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL**:  
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume}
   \]  
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = 0.044 \text{ g/100 mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.044 \times 10 = 0.044 \text{ g}
   \]  
4. **Convert grams to milligrams**:  
   \(
   1 \text{ g} = 1000 \text{ mg}
   \]  
   \[
   0.044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 44 \text{ mg}
   \]  
   Thus, there are \(\boxed{44 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
