   \text{Molarity} = \frac{\text{Normality} \times \text{H}_3\text{PO}_4 \text{ equivalents per mole}}{\text{H}_3\text{PO}_4 \text{ protons per molecule}}
   \]
   For H\(_2\)SO\(_4\), the number of protons per molecule is 2, so the equivalental mass is 2.
   \[
   \text{Molarity} = 2.00 \text{ N} \times \frac{2 \text{ equivalents per mole}}{1 \text{ proton per molecule}} = 4.00 \text{ M}
