What is the number of chloride ions produced when the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` (tetraamminedichloroplatinum(IV) chloride) is dissolved in an aqueous solution?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The complex is \[Pt(NH_3}^4\)Cl_2\)Cl_2]. When this complex is dissolved in an aqueous solution, the complex dissociates into its constituent ions. The complex itself dissociates into \(Pt^{2+}\(, \(NH_3^{--}\), and \(Cl^-\). The \(Cl_2\) part dissociates into two \(Cl^-\) ions. Thus, the total number of chloride ions is:
\[
\text{Cl}^-\ \text{from complex} + \text{Cl}^-\ \text{from }Cl_2 = 2 + 2 = 4
\]
The complex \(Pt(NH_3)^4Cl_2\) dissociates into \(Pt^{2+}\), \(4NH_3\), and \(2Cl^-\). The \(Cl_2\) part dissociates into two \(Cl^-\) ions. Thus, the total number of chloride ions is:
\[
