5. Soil compaction: The repeated use of biomass as a renewable energy source can lead to soil compaction, which can reduce water infiltration and root growth.

In conclusion, the use of biomass as a renewable energy source can have both positive and negative impacts on the chemical composition and pH levels of the soil in agricultural areas. It is essential to consider these impacts when using biomass as a renewable energy source and to implement appropriate management practices to minimize any negative effects.
