","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2}^-) \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the following products are precipitated:
1. **\( \text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Mn}^{2+}\)**: The reaction is:
   \[ \text{Mn}^{2+}\text{ + } \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{MgS(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \]
   \( \text{MgS} \) is precipitated.
2. **\( \text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Ni}^{2+}\)**: The reaction is:
   \[ \text{Ni}^{2+}\text{ + } \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{NiS(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \]
   \( \text{NiS} \) is precipitated.
3. **\( \text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Cu}^{2+}\)**: The reaction is:
   \[ \text{Cu}^{2+}\text{ + } \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{CuS(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \]
   \( \text{CuS} \) is precipitated.
4. **\( \text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Hg}^{2+}\)**: The reaction is:
   \[ \text{Hg}^{2+}\text{ + } \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{HgS(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \]
   \( \text{HgS} \) is precipitated.

Thus, all the ions (\(\text{Mn}^{2+}\), \(\text{Ni}^2+\), \(\text{Cu}^2+\), and \(\text{Hg}^2+\)) form precipitates with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) in an acidified aqueous solution.

The precipitates are:
- \(\text{MgS}\) (white)
- \(\text{NiS}\) (yellow)
- \(\HgS}\) (green)
- \(\text{HgS}\) (green)

Final Answer:
