Thus, the difference in refractive indices is:

\[
n_{\text{eff}} - n_f = 0.3
\]

The wavelength is given as \(l = 1 \, \mu\text{m} = 1 \times 1{0^{-6}\text{ m}}\).

Substituting these values into the formula for the decay length:

\[
L = \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{2\pi (0.3)} = \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{0.6 \pi} \approx \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{0.6 \times 3.17} \approx \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{1.91} \approx 0.525 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{m} = 525 \, \mu\text{m}
