The index of refraction is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum to the speed of light in a medium.  
\[
n = \frac{v_1}{v_2}
\]
where \( v_1 \) is the speed of light in the vacuum and \( v_2 \) is the speed of light in the medium.  
In this case, the speed of light in the plastic is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum.  
Thus, \( v_2 = 0.680 v_1 \).  
The index of refraction is:  
\[
n = \frac{v_1}{v_2} = \frac{v_1}{0.680 v_1} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.535
\]  
The index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is \(\boxed{1.535}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

